          "case": "iff-forward",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Example of Worked mathematical example B07 — subtraction and a factorial series: In the QX09 subtraction choose $\\mu_R=\\mu$. Its subtracted coefficient tends to zero, while the positive bare integral grows quadratically: $I_\\Lambda/\\Lambda^2\\to1/(16\\pi^2)$. This zero is determined by the selected subtraction scale and does not assert zero fluctuations or existence of a continuum theory. For the separate toy integral $F(\\lambda)$, every finite coefficient $n!$ exists, but the formal series diverges for every $\\lambda>0$. The forward iff axis adds no separately stated converse hypothesis here; the recorded claim is the displayed construction, identity, implication or scope qualification, not a characterization by a new necessary-and-sufficient condition."
